new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1f02b91
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/availability-mcodes/README
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+AUTO M54/M55 barriers: prior motion drains, ACK wait, held-position validation,
+required homing wait, release wait, and failure prevents continuation.
+Runs with interpolation rate 4 and releases the joint just moved, checking a fixed command and successful unrelated motion. Home All skips unavailable availability-controlled joints; any unhomed controlled joint is homed individually inside M54 before the program may continue. Invalid but syntactically representable selectors are passed through the interpreter and rejected against authoritative task topology. A second run confirms acquisition homing with forced homing disabled, then covers direct nonvolatile reacquisition.
+Abort in AUTO during ACK wait and moving acquisition homing terminates the program. Late ACK never enables the joint or executes the following block; a new program can reacquire and home.
+Machine Off during acquisition homing cancels it like Abort. Stop during M54 acquisition homing behaves like Stop during G28.2: it stays STOPPING until homing ends, then holds the next block until Resume.
+
+INI fixtures are generated by test.sh from the shared FIXTURE.BASE and local
+*.ini.in overrides. Run python3 ../runtime-availability/make-fixtures.py before
+launching an individual case directly. @unset explicitly removes an inherited
+key. Generated INIs are ignored; edit the base or the case override instead.
